{
  // protocol/types.ts is the M1a-2 API surface: its exports are the deliverable,
  // consumed by the M1a-3 / M1a-7 ports (not dead code), so knip's
  // "unused export" check doesn't apply to it.
  //
  // knip emits a "Remove from ignore" hint now that M1a-3's protocol/agent.ts
  // consumes part of this file. Declined: the remaining ~50 exports are typed
  // ahead of their consumers on purpose, and acting on the hint reports every
  // one of them as dead code.
  //
  // core/ids.ts and core/runfile.ts were ignored here while they were typed
  // ahead of their consumers. M1b-2 landed: cli.ts --file reaches core/run.ts,
  // which imports runfile.ts, which imports ids.ts, so the --production pass
  // now finds both from a real entry. Both entries dropped, as M1b-1 said to.
  //
  // integration/ is the opt-in real-harness suite (npm run test:harness). Its
  // files are entry points by definition — a test runner invokes them — but
  // they are not production entries, so the --production pass reaches them
  // from nowhere and calls all four unused. knip has no notion of a second,
  // opt-in test suite, so they are ignored rather than misdeclared as
  // production roots. `npm run check` still type-checks them.
  "ignore": ["protocol/types.ts", "integration/**"],
  // script(1) is util-linux's, spawned by tests/daemon.test.ts to give `attach`
  // (M2-9) and chat.ts a real pseudo-terminal. A system binary, not an npm one,
  // so nothing lists it. vim is the same: the /term test (M4-13) runs it in
  // the person's shell when the system has it.
  "ignoreBinaries": ["script", "vim"],
  // Entry points. The `!` suffix marks a *production* entry: without it, knip's
  // --production mode (which pi-lens runs) has no roots at all and reports every
  // reachable file — protocol/agent.ts, protocol/registry.ts, render.ts — as unused.
  //
  // knip emits "Remove redundant entry pattern" for the `!` entry, since
  // package.json's `start` script already makes `cli.ts` a dev entry.
  // Declined for the same reason: dropping it re-breaks --production.
  //
  // mock-agent.mjs is a runnable script (`node mock-agent.mjs`, inside the
  // selftest script's --cmd string), not an imported module, and is dev-only.
  // hostile-agent.mjs is the same shape: spawned by protocol/tests/hostile.test.ts
  // as a subprocess, never imported, so nothing reaches it through the graph.
  //
  // daemon.ts (M2-1) is the second production root: `node daemon.ts` runs it,
  // and nothing imports it — tests/daemon.test.ts spawns it as a subprocess.
  // chat.ts (chat MVP) is the third, for the same reason: `node chat.ts`, spawned
  // by tests/daemon.test.ts, imported by nothing.
  "entry": [
    "cli.ts!",
    "daemon.ts!",
    "chat.ts!",
    "mock-agent.mjs",
    "hostile-agent.mjs"
  ]
}
